### Step 1: Calculate the molar mass of DCM (\(CH_{2}Cl_{2}\))

Molar mass of \(CH_{2}Cl_{2}\) = (1 \(\times\) atomic mass of C) + (2 \(\times\) atomic mass of H) + (2 \(\times\) atomic mass of Cl)
\text{Molar mass} = 12 + (2 \times 1) + (2 \times 35.5)
\text{Molar mass} = 12 + 2 + 71 = 85 \text{ g/mol}

### Step 2: Calculate the mmoles of DCM

The solution is \(2.6 \times 10^{-3}M\) in \(CH_{2}Cl_{2}\) and the volume of chloroform is 671.141 mL. Assuming the volume of the solution is approximately the volume of chloroform (since DCM is added to chloroform to prepare the solution), we can calculate the moles of DCM.
\text{Moles of DCM} = \text{Molarity} \times \text{Volume (in L)}
\text{Moles of DCM} = 2.6 \times 10^{-3} \text{ mol/L} \times 671.141 \times 10^{-3} \text{ L}
\text{mmoles of DCM} = 671.141 \times 2.6 \times 10^{-3}

### Step 3: Calculate the mass of DCM

\text{Mass of DCM} = \text{Moles of DCM} \times \text{Molar mass of DCM}
\text{Mass of DCM} = (671.141 \times 2.6 \times 10^{-3}) \text{ mmol} \times 85 \text{ g/mol} \times 10^{-3} \text{ mol/mmol}
\text{Mass of DCM} = 671.141 \times 2.6 \times 10^{-3} \times 85 \times 10^{-3} \text{ g}

### Step 4: Calculate the mass of chloroform (\(CHCl_{3}\))

Given density of \(CHCl_{3}\) = \(1.49\) g \(cm^{-3}\) and volume = 671.141 mL.
\text{Mass of } CHCl_{3} = \text{Density} \times \text{Volume}
\text{Mass of } CHCl_{3} = 1.49 \text{ g/mL} \times 671.141 \text{ mL}
\text{Mass of } CHCl_{3} = 1.49 \times 671.141 \text{ g}

### Step 5: Calculate the mass of the solution

Assuming the mass of the solution is approximately the mass of chloroform, as DCM is present in trace amounts.
\text{Mass of solution} \approx \text{Mass of } CHCl_{3} = 1.49 \times 671.141 \text{ g}

### Step 6: Calculate the concentration in ppm (by mass)

\text{PPM (by mass)} = \frac{\text{Mass of solute}}{\text{Mass of solution}} \times 10^6
\text{PPM} = \frac{(671.141 \times 2.6 \times 10^{-3} \times 85 \times 10^{-3})}{(1.49 \times 671.141)} \times 10^6
\text{PPM} = \frac{2.6 \times 10^{-3} \times 85 \times 10^{-3}}{1.49} \times 10^6
\text{PPM} = \frac{2.6 \times 85}{1.49} \times 10^{-6} \times 10^6
\text{PPM} = \frac{221}{1.49}
\text{PPM} \approx 148.322

