### Step 1: Identify given values and simplify terms

z = 1 + i
\bar{z} = 1 - i
i\bar{z} = i(1 - i) = i - i^2 = i + 1
\frac{1}{z} = \frac{1}{1 + i} = \frac{1 - i}{(1 + i)(1 - i)} = \frac{1 - i}{1 - i^2} = \frac{1 - i}{2}

### Step 2: Substitute values into the expression for \(z_{1}\)

z_{1} = \frac{1 + i\bar{z}}{\bar{z}(1 - z) + \frac{1}{z}}
\text{Numerator} = 1 + i\bar{z} = 1 + (1 + i) = 2 + i
\text{Denominator} = \bar{z}(1 - z) + \frac{1}{z}
1 - z = 1 - (1 + i) = -i
\bar{z}(1 - z) = (1 - i)(-i) = -i + i^2 = -1 - i
\text{Denominator} = (-1 - i) + \frac{1 - i}{2} = \frac{-2 - 2i + 1 - i}{2} = \frac{-1 - 3i}{2}
z_{1} = \frac{2 + i}{\frac{-1 - 3i}{2}} = \frac{2(2 + i)}{-(1 + 3i)} = \frac{-2(2 + i)}{1 + 3i}

### Step 3: Rationalize \(z_{1}\)

z_{1} = \frac{-2(2 + i)}{1 + 3i} \times \frac{1 - 3i}{1 - 3i}
z_{1} = \frac{-2(2 - 6i + i - 3i^2)}{1^2 - (3i)^2}
z_{1} = \frac{-2(2 - 5i + 3)}{1 - 9i^2}
z_{1} = \frac{-2(5 - 5i)}{1 + 9}
z_{1} = \frac{-(5 - 5i)}{5}
z_{1} = -1 + i

### Step 4: Calculate \(\arg(z_{1})\)

Since \(z_{1} = -1 + i\) is in the second quadrant, its argument is given by:
\arg(z_{1}) = \pi - \tan^{-1}\left(\left|\frac{\text{Im}(z_{1})}{\text{Re}(z_{1})}\right|\right)
\arg(z_{1}) = \pi - \tan^{-1}\left(\left|\frac{1}{-1}\right|\right)
\arg(z_{1}) = \pi - \tan^{-1}(1)
\arg(z_{1}) = \pi - \frac{\pi}{4}
\arg(z_{1}) = \frac{3\pi}{4}

### Step 5: Calculate the final expression

\frac{12}{\pi}\arg(z_{1}) = \frac{12}{\pi} \times \frac{3\pi}{4}
= \frac{12 \times 3}{4}
= 3 \times 3
= 9

